# Testing Patterns for Bun Test

## Test Structure

### Use Proper Imports

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Bun test imports
import { describe, test, expect, beforeEach, afterEach, beforeAll, afterAll } from 'bun:test';

// ❌ WRONG - Don't use Vitest/Jest
import { describe, test, expect } from 'vitest';
import { describe, test, expect } from '@jest/globals';
```

## Process Cleanup in Tests

**ALWAYS cleanup spawned processes:**

```typescript
import processManager from '../utils/process-cleanup';

describe('My Test Suite', () => {
  // Cleanup after EACH test
  afterEach(async () => {
    await processManager.killAll(3000);
  });
  
  // Or cleanup after ALL tests
  afterAll(async () => {
    await processManager.killAll(3000);
  });
});
```

## Test Timeouts

### Global Timeout (bunfig.toml)

```toml
[test]
timeout = 10000  # 10 seconds default
```

### Per-Test Timeout

```typescript
test('long running test', async () => {
  // Test code
}, { timeout: 30000 }); // 30 seconds
```

### Command Line Timeout

```bash
bun test --timeout 20000
```

## Mock Environment Setup

### Cloudflare Environment Mocks

```typescript
const mockEnv = {
  ANALYTICS: {
    prepare: (query: string) => ({
      bind: (...params: any[]) => ({
        first: async () => null,
        all: async () => ({ results: [] }),
        run: async () => ({ success: true })
      }),
      first: async () => null,
      all: async () => ({ results: [] }),
      run: async () => ({ success: true })
    })
  },
  LINE_INGRESS: {
    send: async (messages: any[]) => ({ success: true })
  },
  ANALYTICS_ENGINE: {
    writeDataPoint: async (data: any) => ({ success: true })
  }
};
```

